# A hardware keyboard's modifier keys in a page's text field (cavekit-input-bridging.md R2; found by the review of
# T-658): Shift, Ctrl and Alt are keys of their own on this device (raw 0x80-0x83) and went into a focused field
# as U+0080-U+0083; Shift+Tab never went backward (the mask's Shift is 0x80, not npPalm's 4).
id: keyboard-modifiers
section: Keyboard and text
item: A hardware keyboard's Shift, Ctrl and Alt pressed alone put nothing in a page's field, Shift+b types B, and Shift+Tab moves the focus back to the field before
shells: enyo mochi mojo
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-input-echo.html
kit: cavekit-input-bridging.md R2
fixture: kernel-kbd
wait rect plain 20
calibrate 'sel:#plain'
tap plain
expect keyboard up
pause 1500
kernel-key 42
kernel-key 29
kernel-key 56
kernel-chord 42 48
wait text echo 'plain n=1 c=0 last=[B] value=[B]' 5
kernel-key 15
wait text echo 'focus=area' 5
kernel-chord 42 15
wait text echo 'focus=plain' 5
